Subject: Tone placement: compare vowels as typed letters, not raw keys (fixes MS layout uyê: huyền, khuyên)

In the MS layout ê is a directly typed key (3), so the EnglishMode flatten saw "uy3"
and the uyê rule never matched; the tone went to y. Use VietnameseMode|MarkLess instead.
Apply with: patch -p1 < this file (from the bamboo-core dir), after 0004.

--- a/bamboo_utils.go
+++ b/bamboo_utils.go
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 			} else if stdStyle {
 				target = vowels[0]
 			} else {
-				var str = Flatten(vowels, EnglishMode|LowerCase|ToneLess|MarkLess)
+				var str = Flatten(vowels, VietnameseMode|LowerCase|ToneLess|MarkLess)
 				if str == "oa" || str == "oe" || str == "uy" || str == "ue" || str == "uo" {
 					target = vowels[1]
 				} else {
